  "rule": "The grid is a lattice of 3x3 tiles separated by 1-cell divider lines. The divider colour is the top-left corner colour. Most tiles share a normal pattern. A few tiles share a special pattern that adds one new colour. The cells of that new colour form a 3x3 mask. Find the unique translation of the mask, at lattice scale, that covers every existing special tile. Stamp the special tile on the remaining mask cells.",
  "scope": "Complete the lattice-scale copy of a shape encoded by the unique new colour inside a special3x3 tile. Infer its unique translation from partial special tiles, then stamp all missing mask positions.",
  "constraints": [
    "All four canonical fixtures reconstruct exactly;1,000 independent archived-solver seeds produce1,000 distinct inputs.",
