  "authored_scope": "Supported: 3x3 tiles with 1-cell dividers and border. Lattices of 4..7 tiles per side; 7x7 (29x29) is drawn with probability 1/2 by default, and smaller or rectangular lattices are synthetic extensions. Random divider, normal and new colours with no collisions. 2- or 3-colour normal tiles, often symmetric. Random 8-connected masks of 3..8 cells that fill the 3x3 box. Three styles for the special tile's background. Any in-bounds offset. Shown subsets of size 2..|mask|-1 that are unique under all translations, contiguous or scattered. Deliberately not supported: lattices larger than 7 (they exceed 30 cells); fewer than 4 tiles per side; tile sizes other than 3x3; masks that do not fill their box; more than one special pattern; placements that only the lattice edge disambiguates.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "The divider colour does not appear in either tile, so only true divider rows and columns are uniform in that colour.",
    "The special tile adds exactly one colour absent from the normal tile. The mask is that colour's cells, has 3..8 cells, is 8-connected and fills the 3x3 box.",
    "Shown is a proper subset of the mask with at least 2 cells, so the output always differs from the input.",
    "No nonzero translation of the mask in [-2,2]^2 covers the shown cells. The placement is unique even if off-lattice translations are allowed, which implies uniqueness among in-bounds offsets.",
    "The offset keeps the whole mask inside the lattice.",
    "Normal tiles are a strict majority: at least 16 tiles, with at most 7 shown.",
    "Explicit parameters are validated. Bools and non-integers are rejected, never coerced. Inconsistent partial specifications raise ValueError."
  ],
